{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2186-09-19 18:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2186-09-19 18:06:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I’ve been having excruciating abdominal pain for the last 10 days. It’s worse than it’s been in months. I need IV Dilaudid — it’s the only thing that works."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2186-09-19 18:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve had chronic pain for a long time, especially with your history of sclerosing mesenteritis and multiple surgeries. Can you describe the pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2186-09-19 18:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s sharp, in my upper belly, and goes down in a V-shape toward my belly button. I’ve also been nauseous and threw up a few times. I had one formed bowel movement in the ER, but it’s not helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2186-09-19 18:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. I see you were given IV Dilaudid and Phenergan in the ER. We’ll monitor your pain and nausea. We also have a CT from outside that shows a partial small bowel obstruction, likely from scar tissue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2186-09-19 18:11:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I need the same IV pain treatment I’ve had before — Dilaudid every 6 hours for several days, then a taper. Why can’t I get that now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2186-09-19 18:12:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We reviewed your case with your outpatient pain doctor. Since you’re passing stool and your abdomen is soft, the team feels this isn’t a severe obstruction. We’re concerned about overusing strong narcotics without clear surgical need."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2186-09-19 18:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I know my body. This pain is real. I’ve been in remission before when I used medical marijuana — but my supply’s been unreliable lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2186-09-19 18:15:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ll manage your pain with acetaminophen and low-dose IV Dilaudid for now, as we did last time. We’re also using non-medication support like music therapy to help with comfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2186-09-19 18:16:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just want to feel better. And I’ve been having those body twitches again — like seizures, but I don’t lose control. They come when I’m stressed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2186-09-19 18:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your records mention those are pseudoseizures — not dangerous, but related to stress. We’ll keep an eye on them. Let’s focus on stabilizing your gut and pain safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2186-09-20 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your albumin came back normal, which is great — it means you’re well-nourished. You’ve had bowel sounds and no vomiting today. How’s the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2186-09-20 09:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still bad. I haven’t slept. I need Ativan IV and Dilaudid. The current dose isn’t enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2186-09-20 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re holding off on increasing the Dilaudid after consulting your pain specialist. Your exam is benign — soft belly, no signs of surgical emergency. We’re worried about dependency and side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-09-20 09:19:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Then I might as well jump out the window. What’s the point if no one will help me?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-09-20 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear how frustrated you are. But statements like that require us to get extra support. I’m going to call Psychiatry to help us through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-09-20 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Psychiatry has seen you and recommended a 1:1 sitter for now. They agree your distress is real, but they’re concerned about safety when pain treatment is limited."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-09-20 10:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t mean it literally. I’m just in so much pain. Why won’t anyone believe me?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-09-20 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We do believe you’re suffering. But we have to balance pain control with safety. You’ve had this pattern before — when narcotics are limited, these thoughts come up. We want to help you through it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-09-20 10:34:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m stressed — new marriage, money problems, only one car for four of us. But that’s nothing new. It’s the pain that’s worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-09-20 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve requested a social work consult to help with system frustrations. For now, we’ll keep managing pain with acetaminophen, promethazine for nausea, and your home meds like gabapentin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-09-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You had a quiet night. The sitter said you slept a few hours. How are you feeling emotionally today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-09-21 09:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still angry. But I’m not thinking about hurting myself anymore. I just want to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-09-21 09:02:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. Psychiatry will re-evaluate you today. If they agree you’re safe, we can remove the sitter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-09-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my pain? It’s still here. Are you sending me home with nothing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-09-21 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. You’ll go home on your regular pain plan — oral meds like acetaminophen, gabapentin, and your sumatriptan for migraines if needed. We’re adding scheduled acetaminophen and PRN promethazine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-09-21 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No IV Dilaudid at all? Not even a prescription to use if it flares?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-09-21 09:08:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at this time. Your outpatient team feels it’s safer to avoid it unless absolutely necessary. We’ll follow up with your gastroenterologist and pain doctor soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-09-21 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Psychiatry cleared you — no current suicidal thoughts. The sitter can be removed. We’re glad you’re feeling safer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-09-21 14:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I didn’t want to hurt myself. I just felt ignored."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-09-21 14:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We hear you. That’s why we’re setting up follow-ups — with your PCP, GI, and psychiatrist. Your care team wants to support you long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-09-22 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your abdomen is soft, bowel sounds are normal, and you’ve tolerated food. We’re planning for discharge tomorrow if all stays stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-09-22 09:11:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my ankle? I came in with a cast already on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-09-22 09:12:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good point. We did an X-ray. There’s an unclear spot on the fibula — could be a fracture. The cast’s still needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-09-22 09:14:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I need to see ortho when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-09-22 09:15:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll need to follow up with orthopedics within the next week to check healing and possibly replace the cast."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-09-22 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds — like rabeprazole for my reflux? I haven’t gotten it here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2186-09-22 09:18:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s not on our formulary, but it’s on your discharge list. You’ll get it filled at home. Same with your Restasis and Salagen for dry eyes and mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2186-09-22 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my sons — they help me with meds. My husband knows what’s going on too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2186-09-22 09:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ve listed your husband as your emergency contact and healthcare proxy. He can help coordinate care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2186-09-23 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s discharge day. You’re medically stable, your pain is manageable, and psychiatry cleared you. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2186-09-23 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m still upset I didn’t get the IV pain treatment I asked for. But I understand you’re trying to keep me safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2186-09-23 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know it’s frustrating. But your body is responding well to conservative care. If pain worsens, go to the ER or call your doctor — don’t hesitate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2186-09-23 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I start feeling hopeless again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2186-09-23 08:06:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Go to the ER or call your psychiatrist immediately. Your safety is the priority. We’re here for you, even after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2186-09-23 08:07:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll follow up with GI and ortho. And keep taking my aripiprazole and paroxetine like always."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2186-09-23 08:09:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your home meds are all on the list. Take acetaminophen regularly, not just when pain flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2186-09-23 08:10:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I wish things had gone differently, but I appreciate you listening at the end."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2186-09-23 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad you’re going home safe. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2186-09-23 08:13:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Goodbye."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2186-09-19 17:53:00",
    "admission_end": "2186-09-23 18:35:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a complex history of sclerosing mesenteritis, chronic abdominal pain, and psychiatric concerns was admitted for acute worsening of her chronic abdominal pain, with imaging showing a partial small bowel obstruction likely due to adhesions. She required low-dose IV hydromorphone initially but was transitioned to oral acetaminophen and non-pharmacologic support after consultation with her outpatient pain team. Her request for high-dose IV narcotics was not fulfilled due to safety concerns and a benign abdominal exam. This led to transient suicidal ideation, resulting in a 1:1 sitter and psychiatry involvement. After 48 hours, she denied self-harm thoughts and was deemed safe. She also had an ankle fracture in a cast, requiring orthopedic follow-up. She was discharged home with her home medications, including gabapentin and acetaminophen for pain, and instructions to follow up with GI, psychiatry, and orthopedics.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Suicidal ideation",
      "Other convulsions",
      "Irritable bowel syndrome",
      "Dyspepsia and other specified disorders of function of stomach",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Migraine without aura, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Sicca syndrome"
    ]
  }
}
